<% content_for :title, "Terms" %>

<article class="max-w-2xl">
  <header class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">The rules for playing Purple. By making an account, you agree to them.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="space-y-8 leading-relaxed">
    <section aria-labelledby="game">
      <h2 id="game" class="text-xl font-bold">Purple is a training game</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        Purple teaches you to spot and stop cyber attacks by playing both sides. Every company, person,
        message and web address in it is fictional. It's free, it's provided as it is for learning, and
        it isn't professional security advice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="who-can">
      <h2 id="who-can" class="text-xl font-bold">Who can play</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        You need to be 13 or over to make an account. One account per person, and keep your password
        to yourself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="fair">
      <h2 id="fair" class="text-xl font-bold">Play fair</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-ink-muted">
        <li>Don't try to get scores or XP you didn't earn by playing: no scripts, bots or tampering
          with the game's requests.</li>
        <li>Pick a display name that's fine for everyone to see. We may rename or remove accounts with
          offensive names.</li>
        <li>Don't attack, overload or probe the Purple website itself. The attacks belong inside the
          game, against fictional targets. If you find a security problem, please tell us at
          <%= mail_to "privacy@purple.daz.codes", nil, class: "text-purple-team underline" %> instead.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="learned">
      <h2 id="learned" class="text-xl font-bold">Use what you learn for good</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        Red's side teaches how attacks work so you can defend against them. Never use these techniques
        against real people or organisations without their written permission. Doing so can be a
        crime, including under the Computer Misuse Act 1990 and the Fraud Act 2006.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="accounts">
      <h2 id="accounts" class="text-xl font-bold">Your account</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        We may suspend or delete accounts that break these rules. You can ask for your account to be
        deleted at any time (see the <%= link_to "privacy page", privacy_path, class: "text-purple-team underline" %>).
        We may change the game, reset leaderboards between seasons, or stop running Purple. If these
        terms change in a way that matters, we'll say so on the site before the change applies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="liability">
      <h2 id="liability" class="text-xl font-bold">Our responsibility</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        We try to keep Purple running and accurate, but can't promise it will always be available or
        free of mistakes. As far as the law allows, we're not liable for any loss from using it.
        Nothing in these terms limits liability that can't legally be limited, such as for death or
        personal injury caused by negligence, or for fraud.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="contact">
      <h2 id="contact" class="text-xl font-bold">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink-muted">
        Purple is run by Darren Jones. These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales.
        Contact: <%= mail_to "privacy@purple.daz.codes", nil, class: "text-purple-team underline" %>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated 16 November 2026.</p>
  </div>
</article>
